A||||7||Greg Piet||fire extinguisher
Z||000000||Greg Piet||09-02-99||09:12 PM||||I got a fire extinguisher and I am trying to find an appropriate place to put it.<br>My real dilemma is my climate.<br>I am in Las Vegas, and the cabin temp can get  up to 160 deg F on a really hot day, but normally the temp is between 120 and 140 deg F in the summertime.  It is listed not to be stored in excess of 120 deg F.<br>The extinguisher is pressurized to 100 psi but the canister has been tested to 300 psi.<br>In theory the canister will be OK in the hot cabin(increasing the temp by 40 deg F should not cuse the pressure to excees 300 psi), but lets face it theory isnt the same as real life.   <br>Has anyone else installed an extinguisher and if so, where did you place it?<br>If the extinguisher is in the "trunk" it seems rather hard to access in case of emergency.
Z||000001||Patrick||09-02-99||10:15 PM||||<br>I mounted mine up front where the spare tire is supposed to be.<p>The LAST place to put it would be in the engine compartment. <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>
Z||000002||ChadMan||09-03-99||05:48 AM||||I've had an extinguisher in every one of my Fieros.  I'm short (er, I mean, vertically challenged), so I mount them behind the driver's seat on the firewall.  The extinguishers have never exhibited any problem, even on sunny days with temps approaching 100.  If you're under 5'10" you probably have room to do this.<p>In 7.5 years and 100K miles of Fiero motoring, all I've had to extinguish was some kid's Olds 98 (knock on urethane for luck).
Z||000003||Greg Piet||09-03-99||08:29 AM||||Yes Im a bit too tall for mounting behing the drivers seat.  <br>Im not really concerned with putting out my car (im under the decklid so much I would notice and oil leak rather quickly).<p>But out by me there is a racetrack that has open drag night for the general public.  With some of the flak i've taken for the pastic car, I am seriously tempted to throw in a turbo and humiliate a few of the fiero bashers in town.  I just thought a fire extinguisher would be a good idea 'just in case'.
Z||000004||theogre||09-03-99||02:19 PM||||what size bottle you get?<p>Obviously fire bottles have to be built to take quite allot of abuse to be UL approved for moble use. If you have doubts about the one you have see if it's USCG approved for marine use as well.<p>depending on the size, under the dash on the pasenger side of the tank hump would work. Make sure you use really short screws and a stop on the drill bit so you don't punch the tank.
Z||000005||Gokart||09-03-99||05:54 PM||||Didn't even mount mine. Just laid it on top of the spare up front. Never moves!
Z||000006||Cooter||09-03-99||07:39 PM||||I just laid mine behind the passenger side seat and then reclined the seat back to hold it in place. Since I have no friends (due to a recent marriage), it doesnt really matter that the seat cannot slide all the way back.
Z||000007||Eric||09-04-99||06:05 PM||||Ogre, what kind/brand meets these requirements?  I'm thinking of mounting it directly in front of the passenger seat, so it won't limit leg room.
